# The upstream commits CI builds against: build.yml checks each library out into reference\<name> (<NAME> in
# lowercase) and caches reference\ under these commits. reference.yml proposes newer ones in PRs, monthly
# (outside .github/workflows because the workflow token may not change workflow files). The modding
# workspace's own reference\ checkouts should match; tools\build.ps1 warns when they don't.
#
#   <NAME>_REPO   the GitHub repository
#   <NAME>_REF    the pinned commit
#   <NAME>_TAG    its release tag: a newer vX.Y.Z tag is proposed
#   <NAME>_FILES  instead of a tag, for libraries without releases: the files the build uses (comma-separated);
#                 the newest default-branch commit that is a week old is proposed if it changes one of them

# ReShade's add-on API headers and its deps/imgui submodule. ReShade refuses add-ons built against another
# ImGui version, and core/reshade_overlay.cc asserts IMGUI_VERSION_NUM: a release with a new ImGui fails the
# build until CLAUDE.md's "Updating for a new ReShade version" is done.
RESHADE_REPO=crosire/reshade
RESHADE_REF=18deaa52de0c425a78b329e9cb3c497281cd00ec
RESHADE_TAG=v6.8.0
